; Console manifest (Xbox Series X|S / PS5). Must be named exactly like the
; folder. Keep this file and TrialTagger.txt identical apart from this comment.
;
; The PC client reads either extension -- LibAddonMenu ships only a .addon and
; loads on PC fine -- so the pair is not a PC/console split. .addon is what the
; Bethesda.net console submission requires, and .txt is what every PC add-on
; uses and what players and tooling expect to find; we ship both so neither
; audience meets a surprise.
;
; APIVersion must match the live client or the add-on shows as out of date.
; Check it in game with:  /script d(GetAPIVersion())
; Only the first two values on the line are honoured.

## Title: Trial Tagger
## Author: |c3498dbTrial Tagger|r
## Version: 0.1.1
## AddOnVersion: 1
## APIVersion: 101050 101051
## Description: Shows your veteran trial achievements as a checksummed code you can screenshot and post to Discord for automatic role assignment.
## SavedVariables: TrialTaggerSV
;
; Optional, never DependsOn. The library draws console settings panels through
; LibHarvensAddonSettings, which has been pulled from the store before; a hard
; dependency would stop the addon loading at all instead of falling back to the
; /trialtag slash command.
## OptionalDependsOn: LibAddonMenu-2.0

Catalog.lua
Codec.lua
Scanner.lua
UI.lua
Settings.lua
TrialTagger.lua
